WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.970
eyecatch

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:37.390
Yeah?

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.530
Why's our club the way it is?

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.390
What do you mean?

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.400
Well...

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.190
Uh...

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.350
Um...

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:17.550
A class hierarchy.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:17.550
karasu nai hierarukii

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.090
Nobody really decided it,

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.090
sou dare ga kimeta wake demo naku

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:21.430
but suddenly, there were first, second, and third fiddles.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:21.430
itsunomanika tsukuriagerareru itsu-gun ni-gun san-gun

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:23.140
In all cases, ranking from the best of the worst to the worst of the best,

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:23.140
subete ni oi te chuu no ge kara chuu no jou

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.770
our world of delusions is full of excitement.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.770
mousou sekai de mainichi waakyaa

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:25.980
I mean, it's not like I want to become popular.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:25.980
ichi-gun ni naritai wake demo nai

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.440
But so is my second fiddle fantasy.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.440
sonna watashitachi wa ni-gun no fantajiisutaa de aru

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.610
Having delusions is my special skill and my hobby.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.610
tokugi mousou shumi mousou

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.780
Experiencing lovers from as far as Greece.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.780
kyou no koibito girishajin

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:41.120
I've gotta write down this fantasy in my 23rd diary.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:41.120
korede ni-juu-san satsume mousou koukan nikki no ohenji wo kakanakuccha

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.200
I've given up on reality,

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.200
riaru wa mou akirameteru

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.960
but I'm still holding out for a miracle.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.960
mirakuru shinjite wa irukedo

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:55.090
The wait's so painful — fitting for a second fiddle.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:55.090
itakutte choudou nigun no yuutopia

00:01:55.130 --> 00:02:00.890
Whether we're chatting or going to the bathroom together,

00:01:55.130 --> 00:02:00.890
hanashi awase warau toka isshoni toire ikunda toka

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:06.980
I feel like I'm getting in their way, like I don't belong.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:06.980
nandakanda de jama kussasou watashi nyamurida

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:14.110
Just ignore me; I'm kinda busy right now

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:14.110
ima taihen nano watashi no koto megutte

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:19.820
because my upperclassman, prince, and musician are having a huge fight.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:19.820
senpai to onzoushi to muujishan ga ookenka

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:26.160
Acting out scenes from manga with my "friends" is so much fun.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:26.160
tomodachi to manga saigen ano serifu chou iiyo ne

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:32.460
They're on a completely different level than the guys in my class, with their silky hair.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:32.460
kurasu ni aru danshi towa reberu chigau yo ne kaminoke sarasara dashi

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:39.170
My delusion diary remains a complete secret from everyone.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:39.170
darenimo zettai himitsu nano watashi no mousou nikki-chou

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:45.890
What love should I experience tomorrow?

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:45.890
ashita wa donna koi shiyou

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:52.940
Two Years Ago

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:04.490
Club

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:10.830
Seriously! What is going on?

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:16.940
What's the big idea? Who are you?
Where am I? And why did this happen?

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:19.980
Four whole questions, huh? Aren't you an inquisitive one?

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:20.680
Huh?

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:30.890
Uh, can I ask why I was kidnapped?

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.680
This ain't a kidnapping!

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.400
It's our club's time-honored initiation ceremony!

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.140
I apologize for the rough treatment.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:42.910
If you don't mind, why don't you hear what we have to say?

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:46.710
We've got tea! Teacakes, too!

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:50.200
Honey-covered pancakes and waffles, to be exact!

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:56.380
Smells good. Kirara like.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:01.380
Huh?

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:04.090
I see. You too, huh?

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:07.930
Just like me, you were kidnapped and forced into the club.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:14.690
Yeah. After going through that once,
I thought it'd never happen again, but...

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.610
Well...

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.530
Man, you're getting annoying. What's the problem?

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:24.160
This is the GJ Club's room, right?

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.780
Duh. That's why you're wearing a school uniform.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:32.040
But, uh, we aren't in Japan, are we?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:36.040
Use your eyes. We're in New York.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.190
Oh, totally! Yeah, New York!

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:42.770
I dunno what I'd do if we were somewhere else...

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:44.800
<i>Wait.</i>

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:48.810
<i>What?!</i>

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:53.400
N-New York? Like, <i>the</i> New York? The one in America?

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.060
What, is there a different one?

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:59.870
I mean, I do recall being trapped in that bag for a significant amount of time,

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:01.440
but why <i>New York</i>?

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.450
It's lost time.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.570
Lost time?

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:07.700
Kyolo-kun.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:13.660
Didn't we forget to do something important?

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.250
Something important?

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:17.580
A graduation trip!

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.130
Come again?

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.130
Kyolo. On graduation trip.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:28.930
Uh, I think this is something that should be for graduates only,

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:30.850
like Kirara,

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.850
Shion-san,

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.310
and the Prez.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:36.770
Who you calling the Prez?

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:40.400
Oh, right. You've graduated, so...

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.480
But this time's an exception.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:45.740
Didn't I tell you? We're making up for lost time.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.490
The GJ Club's lost time.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:52.330
Oh, so that's what's going on? Explains why we're all in uniforms, in the clubroom...

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:56.040
But why's the clubroom here? Did someone just drag and drop it to New York?

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:06.170
Mori-san did all the work.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:08.430
Ah...

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.680
Um...

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:16.180
If you don't mind me asking, why New York?

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:18.140
You've got a brain, don't you?

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.190
You should be able to figure it out.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:23.190
New York's shortened to NY, right?

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:27.070
And our club's GJ. Both are two letters.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:28.820
Is that it?

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:31.990
I mean, Los Angeles works too, right?

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:35.750
You could even say we'd be making up for <i>Los</i> time.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.880
We'll pretend we never heard that, okay?

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.260
My apologies...

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:56.060
Oh yeah, I'm a JK, right?

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:59.350
I think people might get the wrong idea if you call yourself a "juvenile knockout"...

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:03.980
Someone once told me: "When you become an adult, things will work themselves out."

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:05.900
Uh, what?

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:09.860
Automatic doors! That's what I've been talking about this whole time.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.070
I highly doubt that...

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:14.450
Automatic doors are my natural enemy.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:18.080
<i>Open! Open, I say! It's Tama! Open sesame! Open!</i>

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:16.540
They always ignore my existence.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.080
What, they don't open?

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.870
And thus, I can't enter convenience stores.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:22.540
And thus, I can't buy potato chips.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.210
And thus, I end up stealing yours.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:28.130
You should just buy your own...

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.550
But does that really happen?

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:31.970
Indeed. It does.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:36.970
Erase your existence. Doors won't open.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:40.350
Erase your existence?

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:43.980
So to make them notice me, I'm wearing these bells.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.820
But they still don't open!

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.990
So that's the story behind those bells.

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:54.070
When I was little, I was told that they'd open once I'm grown up.

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:58.160
Well, some older automatic doors open if you step on the mat.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:00.620
But I guess kids don't weigh enough.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.790
You ever encounter this problem?

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.460
Why're you asking me?

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:07.460
If you can't open them yourself, then how do you get in?

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.460
I wait by the entrance.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:13.050
As soon as someone else comes, I sneak in.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.260
I see.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:17.140
The same goes for leaving the place, too.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:21.430
If I don't make it out in time, the doors attack me.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:23.520
Sounds rough.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:26.480
Does anyone want a refill?

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:42.660
All right! Let's do something <i>American</i>!

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:45.210
Something American?

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:48.590
You're good as you are, Kirara. You're plenty American.

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:49.210
Huh?

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:52.720
Look at you, digging into the meat on the bone. Talk about wild!

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.470
You're totally American!

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.510
Kirara is Kirara.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:01.310
That's right, Megu! There's, like, American coffee, right?

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:03.230
So brew us some American tea!

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:05.600
Sounds good!

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.350
American tea...

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:10.860
Tama, you're set as well.
I mean, your attitude just <i>speaks</i> freedom!

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:14.740
But I'm a maiden. Japanese ideals in the flesh.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:17.990
Shii, you're rocking the Harvard-ness.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.700
That's not exactly in New York...

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.790
Like this?

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:24.620
Perfecto!

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:26.750
Really?

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:29.880
C'mon, you get in the American groove, too!

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:31.630
That's a tall order...

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:35.840
Even if you're a beta, you've gotta go full alpha in the States!

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:40.680
We're talking buff steaks, fried chicken, tasty hot dogs, and some BBQ!

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.350
That got you hungry, didn't it?

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:51.610
It's almost lunchtime, ain't it? Let's eat.

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:55.240
Steaks would be a little heavy for lunch,
so how about some hamburgers?

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:57.570
Hamburgers!

00:09:58.740 --> 00:09:59.820
Meat!

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:02.910
Let's have hamburgers for lunch then!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:06.120
The burgers over here are crazy, you know? They're the real deal, after all!

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:09.170
A real hamburger...

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:11.210
I can't wait!

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:15.210
They're, like, humongous!
Loaded with thousands of calories!

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:16.420
No!

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:21.220
I don't get fat, so that doesn't matter to me.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:23.970
That's not fair, Tama-chan!

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:25.350
Meat!

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.410
Why's our club...

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:55.750
the way it is?

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:58.590
What do you mean?

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:04.890
One of my former classmates once told me:

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:08.230
"Your club's so chillaxed!"

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.560
Chillaxed?

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.150
Yup. Chillaxed.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:15.980
Then again, it also gets pretty hectic around here.

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:19.570
Hey, I like it! Let's all strive to be chillaxed!

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:21.660
Strive to be chillaxed?

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:24.530
Why don't we call it "the way of chillaxedness"?

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:26.740
That's it! It's the way of chillaxedness!

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.290
Chillaxed, huh?

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:34.000
I don't approve of slapping "the way" onto everything.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:38.510
Seeing and hearing about "the way of God" at the shrine is more than enough.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:45.300
We're out of chips, Senpai. Go buy some more.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:47.890
The burgers we ordered should arrive soon. Just wait a bit.

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:49.270
Hamburgers!

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:52.850
It is said that the delicate patty of meat wrapped between the buns

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:57.360
was originally the on-the-road food of choice of equestrian nomads

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:59.570
before it was adopted by Americans during the advance of Western Europe.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:03.990
Well, Shion-sama's sure got high hopes.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:10.040
They'll be here soon. Food delivery in America is known to be quick, right?

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.620
With some person zooming around on a motorcycle?

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:16.290
Yeah, yeah! And a big bike at that!

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:28.970
Hey, that should be them.

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:29.930
You're probably right!

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:30.850
We are the GJ Club!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:38.480
Sorry to keep you waiting, Onii-chan!

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:41.780
<i>Hope you weren't waiting long, my samurai master.</i>

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:38.520
Hope you weren't waiting long,
     my samurai master.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.660
I do hope the wait was bearable, Kyouya-sama.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:41.900
Hope you weren't waiting long,
     my samurai master.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:47.780
<i>Making middle school girls dress up like this...</i>

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:51.790
<i>Your perversion astounds me, you scum.</i>

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.830
Hey, I had nothing to do with this.

00:12:53.830 --> 00:13:01.210
Hope you weren't waiting long,
     my samurai master.

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:57.040
Wait, you girls came, too? To New York?

00:12:57.040 --> 00:13:01.210
As your little sister, it's my duty to watch over you at all times!

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:04.510
Right... But what's with the outfits?

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:06.680
This is what a delivery's supposed to be like!

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.680
Complete with clumsy waitresses!

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:11.890
We're here to clumsy it up!

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:14.640
Clumsy, clumsy, spinny, spinny!

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:16.560
I believe we ordered burgers, not ditzes...

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:20.230
Wait, how did you know we ordered something, anyway?

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:22.690
And where have you three been up until now?

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:25.530
Man, the Statue of Liberty was amazing!

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:22.740
Central Park was
lovely, with its luscious
green landscapes.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:28.870
<i>Central Park was lovely, with its luscious green landscapes.</i>

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:25.570
Central Park was
lovely, with its luscious
green landscapes.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:31.950
The Broadway musical wasn't half bad either.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:28.910
Central Park was
lovely, with its luscious
green landscapes.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:35.210
So you've been having fun touring around New York...

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:31.990
Central Park was
lovely, with its luscious
green landscapes.

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:39.460
To be fair, the normal thing to do in a foreign place is to sightsee.

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:45.550
Kasumi-chan, you look totally adorbs!

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:47.800
Maa-chan!

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:50.350
So cute! You look like a doll!

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:52.060
Thanksies, Kasumi-chan!

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.180
So even after you graduate,
you're gonna continue the Maa-chan thing?

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:59.150
Hey, Maa-chan, let's go outside!

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:01.110
A trip outdoors? That's so exciting!

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:04.230
You're on escort duty, Onii-chan.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:01.190
Hello, hello!

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:08.360
I haven't even taken a step outside yet...

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:04.280
Hello, hello!

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:10.120
The hamburger...

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:08.530
Hello, hello!

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:12.530
Some consider it America's national food.

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:16.620
A simple dish, comprising of, at a base level,
a patty and two pieces of bread called "buns."

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:21.630
However, the varieties are endless, and the international expansion of the dish only fanned the flames.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:24.880
This ain't good. Shion-sama's approaching her limit.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:25.920
What?

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:28.720
Don't worry! She said she'd be here soon.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:29.130
Huh?

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:47.280
My apologies for the delay.

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:49.200
Mori-san!

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.200
Oh, I forgot.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.510
Here's your order.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.510
Hamburgers!

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.890
I had Mori-san make some.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:18.270
With specific attention to the calorie count, too!

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.100
Is that so?

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:23.520
Yeah, we were sightseeing with Mori-san.

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:20.230
And then the call for
burgers came in.

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:26.230
<i>And then the call for burgers came in.</i>

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:23.560
And then the call for
burgers came in.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.860
So we borrowed the hotel's kitchen for a bit.

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:32.870
If we're talking New York, you gotta go for burgers! Can't beat authentic tastes!

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:35.870
If Mori-san made them, I don't think they're authentic.

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.870
Shut up! Location matters, man!

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:43.210
Is it time? Can we eat them now?

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:45.130
Shion-san?

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:47.170
Whoa, Shii! Down, down!

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:50.260
All right, everybody. Let's dig in!

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:51.470
Ready, and...

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:53.760
Thanks for the food!

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:57.600
F-From what I remember, hamburgers are eaten in a single bite like this...

00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:59.770
Take the wrapper off first!

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.750
Meat! Meatie, meatie!

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:38.600
Hamburgers...

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:40.600
I ate too much.

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:42.890
Here you go, Shinomiya-sama.

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:44.850
Oh, thank you.

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:47.900
You're always supporting us.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:50.730
It's my job, after all.

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:57.620
We're still missing something critical.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:01.200
The desserts! Where are the desserts?

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.660
You're still hungry?

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.830
Very well. Allow me to prepare—

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:06.380
Hold that thought!

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:09.880
You guys seem to be forgetting something important!

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:11.630
Something important?

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:14.380
Where are we right now? New York, right?

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:15.380
Yeah...

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:18.390
New York's the <i>origin</i> of this, guys!

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:21.140
We're talking Halloween!

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:24.310
Wait, seriously?

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.480
Is New York seriously the birthplace of Halloween?

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:32.940
With that in mind, the GJ Club's gonna grab their dessert with their own two hands.

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:35.490
All in the spirit of Halloween, of course.

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:38.200
But today's not Halloween.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:40.530
It's not even October, for that matter.

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:42.870
Awesome! A Halloween competition!

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:45.160
It's time for revenge, Maa-chan!

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.620
Heh. A middle schooler should watch what they say!

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:50.340
But you're in elementary school, aren't you?

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:57.340
With that being said, let's all nab some candy from the city!

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:58.430
Yeah!

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:00.510
Please don't steal any!

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:02.350
All right, time to get changed!

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:03.390
Yeah!

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:05.180
Hey, listen!

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:06.390
Huh?

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:13.030
What?!

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:39.720
Seriously, stop making me do this!

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.720
That one was all you.

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:44.390
Onii-chan... Onee-chan?

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:48.850
A samurai?
A maiden?

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:46.220
<i>A samurai? A maiden?</i>

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:48.850
A fitting outfit for someone like you.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.900
Well, now that Kyoloko has made her appearance,

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:53.650
let's actually get changed!

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:54.190
Yeah!

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:55.860
Wait, is this really happening?

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:59.280
Whoa, don't take off your clothes! I'm still here!

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:01.870
Am I seriously going like this?

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:11.630
What a large haul!

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:15.130
Everyone in New York was so nice!

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:18.470
Can we not do this again?

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:24.970
We finally got to go outside, but
didn't get to sightsee or anything.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:29.480
Well, Maa-chan? I think the middle school division can claim victory!

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:31.310
I'm calling it a tie.

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:32.060
What?

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:35.770
With this, I can retire in peace—

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:44.410
But boy, was Kyoloko ever popular!

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:46.280
C-C'mon, stop it.

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:47.950
Why don't we just go with Kyoloko?

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:49.910
The next president can be her instead of you.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:50.620
Now look here...

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:52.790
Wait, Onii-chan, you're the next president?

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:53.580
Well, kinda—

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:55.960
That's amazing! I can't believe you're the next president!

00:19:54.170 --> 00:20:01.680
Congratulations,

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:58.130
<i>Congratulations, my master.</i>

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:00.880
<i>Abusing your political power to promote perversion, I see.</i>

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:02.130
Whoa, hold on.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:06.680
If you're the president, you've gotta perform
presidential duties. Like buying a new bag of chips.

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:11.020
Onii-chan, fulfill your presidential duty and brush my hair!

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:11.020
I think the GJ Club will be fine.

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:12.390
What?

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:14.600
<i>Is that your true nature, you brute?</i>

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:18.110
<i>M-Master, I want you to brush me, too!</i>

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:18.110
Well, seems like we made up for lost time!

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:22.400
Onii-chan, brush my hair! Brush it!

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.490
Come on, brush it!

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:38.170
Sengawa Theatre

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:52.230
Slow down. No running!

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:06.280
The World Collection

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:26.720
Relaxing

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:30.180
Haven't seen you in a while.

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:36.350
Not since the graduation trip, right?

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:43.990
H-How's college going?

00:21:46.490 --> 00:22:02.000
Relaxing

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:54.330
U-Uh, I was asked by Megumi-chan to grab some tea leaves for her.

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:56.710
Do you come here oft...

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:00.630
Welcome!

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:03.630
Your total comes to 700 yen.

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:05.840
Would you like a bag?

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:09.890
300 yen is your change.

00:22:15.930 --> 00:22:17.730
Thank you for shopping!

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:24.780
Well, see you later.

00:22:24.780 --> 00:22:25.940
Yeah.

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:34.700
Hey, Megumi-chan. I just finished shopping.

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:36.540
Yeah. Yeah.

00:22:37.790 --> 00:22:39.120
What's up, Shii?

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:43.040
By the station? Gotcha.

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:43.040
Sure. By the station, right?

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:55.770
All right. Let's wait ahead for them.

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:56.850
Roger!

00:22:57.680 --> 00:22:59.940
Sengawa Station

00:23:12.820 --> 00:23:14.120
U-Um...

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:21.580
The weather's nice today, isn't it?

00:23:24.340 --> 00:23:27.710
Do you still meet up with Shion-san, even after graduating?

00:23:37.390 --> 00:23:38.770
Shuffle, shuffle, shuffle.

00:23:42.350 --> 00:23:44.150
This is a bit far.

00:23:44.150 --> 00:23:46.730
You're right.

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:49.690
Megu. That's not it.

00:23:49.690 --> 00:23:51.660
Huh? Oh...

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:50.070
Grin

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:51.700
 Parking is prohibited in the areas.
Any unattended motorcycles or bikes will be taken away.

00:23:52.360 --> 00:23:56.080
I can't hear their conversation. Let's get closer.

00:23:52.360 --> 00:23:52.410
 Parking is prohibited in the areas.
Any unattended motorcycles or bikes will be taken away.

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:57.160
Roger.

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:56.120
 Parking is prohibited in the areas.
Any unattended motorcycles or bikes will be taken away.

00:23:59.580 --> 00:24:00.910
She's late.

00:24:00.910 --> 00:24:05.170
Jeez, come on! What the crap is Shii doing?

00:24:22.140 --> 00:24:23.850
H-Huh?

00:24:26.360 --> 00:24:28.730
That was close.

00:24:28.730 --> 00:24:30.740
Much appreciated, Kirara.

00:24:32.780 --> 00:24:36.570
That was Shion-san's ringtone, right?

00:24:36.570 --> 00:24:37.910
I thought so.

00:24:38.240 --> 00:24:40.870
Maybe someone happened to have the same ringtone?

00:24:40.870 --> 00:24:43.370
That doesn't explain why nobody was there.

00:24:43.370 --> 00:24:44.620
They just—

00:24:51.720 --> 00:24:54.840
Um, can I ask you a question?

00:24:56.340 --> 00:25:01.350
Why have you been trying to avoid talking to me?

00:25:05.900 --> 00:25:07.980
Can you at least tell me why?

00:25:12.150 --> 00:25:14.650
Sengawa Station

00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:17.280
I'm...

00:25:17.490 --> 00:25:20.450
Oh? If it ain't the Prez!

00:25:20.450 --> 00:25:22.200
And the mini Prez, too!

00:25:22.200 --> 00:25:24.370
Wh-What's your deal?

00:25:24.370 --> 00:25:26.210
Wh-Why are you here?

00:25:26.580 --> 00:25:30.960
Why not? It's my day off, after all.

00:25:31.670 --> 00:25:34.550
Well, it <i>is</i> the weekend.

00:25:34.550 --> 00:25:37.390
I'm just taking a break from being a big sister.

00:25:37.390 --> 00:25:42.520
If I stay at home, little bro after sis after bro after sis get real annoying, real fast.

00:25:43.930 --> 00:25:46.100
I see...

00:25:47.400 --> 00:25:50.480
Why are you two together, anyway?

00:25:53.230 --> 00:25:56.490
You guys still hang out together often, even after graduating?

00:25:57.070 --> 00:25:59.450
You shouldn't keep secrets from me.

00:26:00.370 --> 00:26:02.540
It's not good to exclude friends from these things!

00:26:02.540 --> 00:26:03.500
Huh?

00:26:03.500 --> 00:26:07.000
C'mon! What's the scoop?

00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:09.210
Tell me!

00:26:09.210 --> 00:26:11.540
Shut your mouth!

00:26:11.540 --> 00:26:14.510
This is the last time you'll see me, you big dunce!

00:26:15.970 --> 00:26:18.090
What bee's in her bonnet?

00:26:18.800 --> 00:26:21.180
Yeah, she's been acting strange for a while.

00:26:21.180 --> 00:26:23.140
I've been wondering if something happened—

00:26:23.140 --> 00:26:24.850
Huh? Tama?

00:26:24.850 --> 00:26:25.520
Where did...

00:26:28.310 --> 00:26:30.310
That was close.

00:26:30.310 --> 00:26:33.530
This calls for a change of plans.

00:26:33.530 --> 00:26:36.530
Sengawa Station

00:26:39.660 --> 00:26:41.990
Megumi-chan's sure late.

00:26:42.700 --> 00:26:45.540
But this is pretty typical for the GJ Club, though.

00:26:48.330 --> 00:26:51.670
<i>This is the last time you'll see me, you big dunce!</i>

00:27:00.550 --> 00:27:02.850
Huh? Megumi-chan?

00:27:03.680 --> 00:27:08.810
South Chofu
   Park

00:27:03.890 --> 00:27:07.730
I'm really sorry. I can't get over to where you are.

00:27:08.820 --> 00:27:11.600
Correct. That park.

00:27:11.600 --> 00:27:13.520
All right, I'll be waiting.

00:27:14.320 --> 00:27:17.240
Let's make this one count.

00:27:17.240 --> 00:27:18.490
You're right.

00:27:18.490 --> 00:27:23.280
Hey, why didn't you guys tell me about this?

00:27:23.280 --> 00:27:25.660
Keeping secrets from friends is bad.

00:27:33.250 --> 00:27:36.210
I think it'll work out fine.

00:27:46.850 --> 00:27:49.230
Where exactly is she, anyway?

00:28:25.050 --> 00:28:26.430
And what's <i>your</i> deal?

00:28:26.930 --> 00:28:29.770
You can't see-saw on your own, right?

00:28:29.770 --> 00:28:33.020
S-Stop acting like you know it all!

00:28:35.690 --> 00:28:37.230
Why you...

00:28:49.120 --> 00:28:50.200
Uh...

00:28:52.620 --> 00:28:54.290
Let me off.

00:29:03.130 --> 00:29:04.260
U-Um...

00:29:12.140 --> 00:29:14.140
What're you guys up to?

00:29:14.140 --> 00:29:16.020
Why are you all...

00:29:16.020 --> 00:29:19.570
I forgot to tell you this when you left the house,

00:29:20.360 --> 00:29:23.320
but we can't go back home tonight.

00:29:23.610 --> 00:29:24.570
Huh?

00:29:24.780 --> 00:29:29.580
Don't worry. Megumi-kun found a good place for us to stay.

00:29:29.580 --> 00:29:31.870
Indeed I did!

00:29:33.290 --> 00:29:34.410
Let's go.

00:29:34.830 --> 00:29:40.130
W-Wait, you guys! Where are we going? Why can't we go home?

00:29:40.130 --> 00:29:44.720
There was a fortune that suggested that we do something different for the night.

00:29:44.720 --> 00:29:48.220
And what's that supposed to mean? You ain't making sense!

00:29:48.220 --> 00:29:51.510
Let. Me. Go!

00:30:15.960 --> 00:30:18.500
What's the big idea, you guys?

00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:23.000
I'm so glad we found a place to sleep.

00:30:23.000 --> 00:30:24.630
In sleeping bags, though?

00:30:24.630 --> 00:30:26.590
Well, I'm not!

00:30:26.590 --> 00:30:31.680
Besides, we aren't allowed to be here.

00:30:31.680 --> 00:30:33.430
That's the rule.

00:30:34.600 --> 00:30:38.940
Graduates of the GJ Club can't go back.

00:30:38.940 --> 00:30:42.690
Today's Sunday, so there's no real club activities taking place.

00:30:42.690 --> 00:30:44.690
That means the rule doesn't apply now, either.

00:30:46.860 --> 00:30:49.320
Uh, why am I here again?

00:30:49.320 --> 00:30:52.030
Isn't it obvious? You're the president of the club!

00:30:52.030 --> 00:30:54.950
I mean, I guess...

00:31:13.470 --> 00:31:16.060
It's been a while, hasn't it?

00:31:16.060 --> 00:31:18.520
Even though it really hasn't been that long...

00:31:18.520 --> 00:31:20.650
Been a while.

00:31:20.650 --> 00:31:26.940
You're right. It's like it was yesterday when you all were still here.

00:31:28.570 --> 00:31:31.200
I always sat over there, right?

00:31:31.950 --> 00:31:34.780
Now I sit over there from time to time!

00:31:34.780 --> 00:31:38.250
You always seemed to be having fun,

00:31:38.750 --> 00:31:40.620
and I wanted in on it!

00:31:40.620 --> 00:31:44.040
Why didn't you say so earlier?

00:31:44.040 --> 00:31:47.630
Come sit on my lap, and I'll teach you some tricks.

00:31:47.630 --> 00:31:49.760
I refuse to sit on your lap!

00:31:51.340 --> 00:31:54.640
Kirara. Sat over there.

00:31:54.640 --> 00:31:58.140
You did, didn't you? All the time, in fact!

00:31:58.350 --> 00:32:00.640
The sun. Felt nice.

00:32:01.060 --> 00:32:03.520
A good spot to lay claim to.

00:32:04.310 --> 00:32:08.070
Come to think of it, Mao took a nap there every now and then.

00:32:08.070 --> 00:32:09.990
She looked so comfy!

00:32:10.740 --> 00:32:14.030
And then we tried to mess with her while she was sleeping.

00:32:14.030 --> 00:32:14.870
Yup.

00:32:14.870 --> 00:32:16.910
Nightmares. Bad.

00:32:18.910 --> 00:32:20.290
U-Um...

00:32:20.290 --> 00:32:22.000
What is it, Kyolo-kun?

00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:28.000
Uh, I was thinking that we should tone it down a bit.

00:32:28.670 --> 00:32:30.470
Why is that?

00:32:30.470 --> 00:32:37.430
Well, there are police officers and
security guards patrolling the halls.

00:32:37.430 --> 00:32:39.520
If they found us here...

00:32:40.480 --> 00:32:41.850
We'd be in for a good scolding.

00:32:44.350 --> 00:32:45.610
Told off.

00:32:47.190 --> 00:32:51.530
And of course we'd be thrown out. No questions asked.

00:32:54.240 --> 00:32:56.070
The GJ Club would be no more.

00:32:57.120 --> 00:32:59.870
At least, that's one possibility.

00:32:59.870 --> 00:33:02.870
Really? Can that happen?

00:33:02.870 --> 00:33:09.300
In order to stay overnight on school grounds,
you need to apply for permission beforehand.

00:33:10.920 --> 00:33:13.840
If you had told me earlier, I would've done it.

00:33:15.130 --> 00:33:17.180
But that ain't fun!

00:33:18.510 --> 00:33:23.480
Going by the rules and doing things normally ain't fun!

00:33:23.480 --> 00:33:26.900
We're having fun <i>'cause</i> we're breaking the rules!

00:33:26.900 --> 00:33:27.980
Shion-san?

00:33:28.230 --> 00:33:31.440
Or at least, that's what Mao would say.

00:33:38.620 --> 00:33:40.660
Just give it a rest.

00:33:41.620 --> 00:33:44.580
What're you even doing, Shii?

00:33:44.580 --> 00:33:47.750
We aren't part of the GJ Club anymore.

00:33:47.750 --> 00:33:50.210
We can't come back here.

00:33:51.050 --> 00:33:52.000
But yet...

00:33:52.000 --> 00:33:53.800
Why...

00:33:54.760 --> 00:33:56.090
Why?

00:34:09.400 --> 00:34:10.730
What's wrong, Kirara?

00:34:12.070 --> 00:34:13.230
Stay quiet.

00:34:46.310 --> 00:34:50.150
This is killing me. Let's just get permission.

00:34:50.650 --> 00:34:54.070
"Nope!"... is what Mao would say.

00:34:54.650 --> 00:34:57.030
I'm not sure I follow...

00:35:05.330 --> 00:35:06.660
U-Um—

00:35:06.660 --> 00:35:07.870
Don't look!

00:35:07.870 --> 00:35:10.370
Just don't! Don't look at me!

00:35:11.290 --> 00:35:12.380
<i>Wait, is this...</i>

00:35:12.500 --> 00:35:14.250
Shut up! Don't look at me!

00:35:18.010 --> 00:35:22.680
You— I... I was scared...

00:35:22.680 --> 00:35:30.390
What if we got caught because of me, and the GJ Club disappeared?

00:35:30.390 --> 00:35:33.770
That'd... That'd just...

00:35:41.950 --> 00:35:43.530
It'll never disappear!

00:35:44.490 --> 00:35:48.290
The GJ Club will never disappear.

00:35:50.000 --> 00:35:55.420
After all, the GJ Club lives in our hearts.

00:35:56.630 --> 00:35:58.800
We <i>are</i> the GJ Club.

00:36:00.380 --> 00:36:05.300
So, don't worry. No matter what, we'll always...

00:36:25.870 --> 00:36:28.870
Ow, ow, ow!

00:36:28.870 --> 00:36:33.920
That hurts! Like, seriously! That legitimately hurts!

00:36:33.920 --> 00:36:37.340
Seriously, it hurts! Stop it!

00:36:44.340 --> 00:36:47.300
Can I get some help over here?

00:36:52.060 --> 00:36:54.850
Fine, whatever!

00:36:54.850 --> 00:36:58.520
Why am <i>I</i> getting worked up over all this, anyway?

00:37:00.070 --> 00:37:00.740
Kyolo!

00:37:01.400 --> 00:37:03.490
<i>You're</i> the president, right?

00:37:03.490 --> 00:37:05.280
Y-Yeah.

00:37:05.660 --> 00:37:08.530
Then you better take responsibility for what'll happen tonight!

00:37:08.530 --> 00:37:10.790
If we get caught, you better shoulder the blame!

00:37:11.040 --> 00:37:15.790
Die with honor and commit seppuku!

00:37:16.040 --> 00:37:18.090
That's your job as the president!

00:37:18.090 --> 00:37:21.380
Um, seppuku might be going too far.

00:37:22.800 --> 00:37:25.380
And you call yourself the president?

00:37:26.390 --> 00:37:29.760
C'mon, stop it! Please!

00:37:29.760 --> 00:37:30.640
Huh?

00:37:31.720 --> 00:37:34.100
Looks like you're back to normal, Mao.

00:37:34.100 --> 00:37:36.480
I was worried about you!

00:37:36.480 --> 00:37:39.150
You've been really depressed recently.

00:37:41.070 --> 00:37:44.650
You guys were up to something from the start, weren't you?

00:37:45.110 --> 00:37:50.200
After Megumi-kun asked, I worked out the plan.

00:37:50.200 --> 00:37:55.330
We thought that if you met Kyolo-kun, you'd think about the GJ Club and be somewhat revitalized,

00:37:55.330 --> 00:37:59.000
but instead, you were stubborn about not talking with him.

00:38:00.710 --> 00:38:04.130
Well, we've graduated, haven't we?

00:38:04.720 --> 00:38:09.970
That's why we're doing this.
To expel that thought from your heart.

00:38:11.600 --> 00:38:13.770
It seems to have worked, though.

00:38:13.770 --> 00:38:16.060
Mao. Full of energy!

00:38:16.060 --> 00:38:19.400
It ain't like the mini Prez to be sulking like that!

00:38:20.230 --> 00:38:22.730
Stop calling me that!

00:38:27.860 --> 00:38:31.660
Feel free to come here whenever you like. We'll welcome you with open arms.

00:38:32.240 --> 00:38:37.370
Like I said, that's not happening. Graduates can't come back.

00:38:37.370 --> 00:38:38.670
And that won't change.

00:38:40.080 --> 00:38:41.130
But...

00:38:41.880 --> 00:38:46.130
You guys will create a new GJ Club from here on out.

00:38:47.590 --> 00:38:48.880
That's how things should be.

00:38:55.310 --> 00:39:00.350
Anyway! It's been a while since I've been here, so why don't we have some fun outside?

00:39:00.730 --> 00:39:04.530
You sure about that? Playing outside the clubroom, I mean.

00:39:04.530 --> 00:39:09.530
If they find us, we'll just run!
And you call yourself a member of the GJ Club?

00:39:09.530 --> 00:39:12.240
Seems like these will be in order.

00:39:12.870 --> 00:39:15.740
I thought that something like this might happen.

00:39:15.740 --> 00:39:17.080
You're on the ball, Megu!

00:39:17.080 --> 00:39:19.830
I brought uniforms for everyone else, too.

00:39:19.830 --> 00:39:21.540
It can actually count as cosplay now.

00:39:21.540 --> 00:39:24.960
Not-so-real high school girls.

00:39:24.960 --> 00:39:28.130
Aight! Let's get this party started!

00:39:28.130 --> 00:39:28.970
Yeah!

00:39:28.970 --> 00:39:30.050
Excuse me!

00:39:33.010 --> 00:39:36.180
You said this at the graduation ceremony, remember?

00:39:37.100 --> 00:39:39.730
That even if we graduate from the GJ Club...

00:39:41.020 --> 00:39:42.560
Our bonds are eternal!

00:39:45.570 --> 00:39:47.070
Right?

00:39:51.070 --> 00:39:56.450
Feel free to contact me.
It doesn't have to be in the clubroom.

00:39:58.120 --> 00:39:59.830
Let's stay in touch,

00:39:59.830 --> 00:40:00.750
Mao.

00:40:04.040 --> 00:40:04.960
Yeah.

00:40:07.960 --> 00:40:11.550
Now then, in alignment with the GJ Club rules, I believe you owe me something, too.

00:40:11.550 --> 00:40:13.510
Kirara next.

00:40:13.510 --> 00:40:16.060
Me too, please!

00:40:16.060 --> 00:40:17.770
Don't forget about me!

00:40:19.980 --> 00:40:22.600
W-We'll worry about that later, you guys!

00:40:22.600 --> 00:40:24.520
But for now, let's have some fun!

00:40:24.730 --> 00:40:26.440
Yeah!

00:40:27.780 --> 00:40:33.280
No, seriously, don't take off your clothes! I'm still here!

00:40:44.830 --> 00:40:50.340
That view we saw together was truly beautiful.

00:40:50.340 --> 00:40:55.760
When I close my eyes, I can easily remember it.

00:40:55.760 --> 00:41:00.680
As we walked down that unfamiliar path together,

00:41:00.680 --> 00:41:06.150
I felt so safe with you by my side.

00:41:06.650 --> 00:41:08.690
The GJ Club was here!

00:41:06.650 --> 00:41:09.400
How nice it would be if someday, somehow,

00:41:08.520 --> 00:41:08.570
The GJ Club was here

00:41:09.400 --> 00:41:11.940
we could soar through the sky.

00:41:09.440 --> 00:41:09.480
The GJ Club was here

00:41:11.940 --> 00:41:17.240
Because then, with a little bit
of magic, I'd become invincible,

00:41:13.740 --> 00:41:19.200
I want to see you now.

00:41:17.410 --> 00:41:22.250
and fly to your world.

00:41:19.830 --> 00:41:22.250
The GJ Club was here!

00:41:22.250 --> 00:41:25.460
But for now, I'll run to where you are,

00:41:25.460 --> 00:41:28.290
regardless of what gets in my way.

00:41:28.290 --> 00:41:33.050
No matter what, I won't cry, because we made a promise.

00:41:33.050 --> 00:41:36.340
I can't stop running, nor can I stop these wishes

00:41:36.340 --> 00:41:39.220
that I've kept in my heart.

00:41:39.220 --> 00:41:43.730
I know they'll be granted someday,

00:41:43.730 --> 00:41:47.270
so be by my side!

00:41:49.860 --> 00:41:55.450
I'll reach out my hand and see what the future holds.

00:41:55.450 --> 00:42:00.870
It'll surely surpass my imagination.

00:42:00.870 --> 00:42:05.960
After all, everything pales in comparison

00:42:05.960 --> 00:42:11.210
to that beautiful smile on your face.

00:42:11.590 --> 00:42:14.470
I should have let you know my feelings earlier,

00:42:14.470 --> 00:42:16.880
but instead, I spent time gazing at the stars.

00:42:17.180 --> 00:42:22.560
Now I'm making my move to see you again,

00:42:18.840 --> 00:42:24.310
It'll all begin soon.

00:42:22.560 --> 00:42:27.310
in the world where you are.

00:42:27.310 --> 00:42:30.630
I've finally arrived, and there you are.

00:42:30.630 --> 00:42:33.400
The sight of you fills me with unimaginable emotion.

00:42:33.400 --> 00:42:38.110
Having longed to see you, the tears of joy flow free.

00:42:38.110 --> 00:42:41.490
I finally arrived, and there you were.

00:42:41.490 --> 00:42:44.240
I'll grab your hand and never let go.

00:42:44.240 --> 00:42:48.790
There's nothing stopping me anymore,

00:42:48.790 --> 00:42:52.800
so be by my side!

00:43:11.270 --> 00:43:14.150
I hate being away from you.

00:43:14.150 --> 00:43:16.650
I want to be the only one in your eyes.

00:43:16.650 --> 00:43:22.200
After all, the time we spend together is truly special.

00:43:18.490 --> 00:43:23.950
It's just not the same.

00:43:22.200 --> 00:43:27.000
It's what defines your world.

00:43:29.670 --> 00:43:32.960
But for now, I'll start running to where you are,

00:43:32.960 --> 00:43:35.750
regardless of what gets in my way.

00:43:35.750 --> 00:43:40.550
No matter what, I won't cry, because we made a promise.

00:43:40.550 --> 00:43:43.800
I can't stop running, nor can I stop these wishes

00:43:43.800 --> 00:43:46.600
that I've kept in my heart.

00:43:46.600 --> 00:43:51.190
I know they'll be granted someday,

00:43:51.190 --> 00:43:54.690
so stay by my side!

00:44:14.540 --> 00:44:20.010
sayonara sabishiku nante

00:44:14.540 --> 00:44:20.010
Goodbyes shouldn't be a sad thing.

00:44:20.010 --> 00:44:25.760
nai kara egao de baibai sa

00:44:20.010 --> 00:44:25.760
I'll say bye-bye with a smile on my face.

00:44:25.760 --> 00:44:30.930
itsumademo kimi ni tayotte nai de

00:44:25.760 --> 00:44:30.930
It's time I stopped always relying on you,

00:44:30.930 --> 00:44:36.190
seichou shita toko misete ageru yo

00:44:30.930 --> 00:44:36.190
and show you I can stand up for myself.

00:44:36.190 --> 00:44:41.610
douyatte douyatte omoi tsutaeyou

00:44:36.190 --> 00:44:41.610
Oh, but how? Oh, but how am I supposed to express myself?

00:44:41.610 --> 00:44:49.450
itsudatte itsudatte kansha shiteta yo arigatou

00:44:41.610 --> 00:44:49.450
After all, after all, I've always been thankful for everything you've done.

00:44:49.790 --> 00:44:52.580
hirogeyou sekaijuu ni

00:44:49.790 --> 00:44:52.580
So let's broaden our horizons

00:44:52.580 --> 00:44:56.420
takusan no warai to namida

00:44:52.580 --> 00:44:56.420
and experience lots of laughs and tears.

00:44:56.420 --> 00:45:00.130
atarashii mirai sa

00:44:56.420 --> 00:45:00.130
It's what the future has in store for us.

00:44:59.740 --> 00:45:01.090
sou

00:44:59.740 --> 00:45:01.090
That's right.

00:45:01.090 --> 00:45:03.800
kimi no pawaa sugokute

00:45:01.090 --> 00:45:03.800
Your power's like the sun;

00:45:03.800 --> 00:45:06.140
minna minna tanoshikute

00:45:03.800 --> 00:45:06.140
everyone around you has fun.

00:45:06.140 --> 00:45:06.850
zutto

00:45:06.140 --> 00:45:08.890
I'm sure

00:45:06.850 --> 00:45:07.600
zutto

00:45:08.890 --> 00:45:11.520
kizuna mahou nokenai yo

00:45:08.890 --> 00:45:11.520
that these bonds won't ever come undone.

00:45:11.520 --> 00:45:14.140
hirogeyou sekaijuu ni

00:45:11.520 --> 00:45:14.140
So let's broaden our horizons

00:45:14.140 --> 00:45:17.980
takusan no warai to namida

00:45:14.140 --> 00:45:17.980
and experience lots of laughs and tears.

00:45:17.980 --> 00:45:21.320
atarashii mirai sa

00:45:17.980 --> 00:45:21.320
It's what the future has in store for us.

00:45:21.320 --> 00:45:22.720
sou

00:45:21.320 --> 00:45:22.720
That's right.

00:45:22.720 --> 00:45:25.410
itsuka kitto mieru hazu

00:45:22.720 --> 00:45:25.410
And pretty soon, you'll see them too:

00:45:25.410 --> 00:45:27.820
jun de kimeta koto

00:45:25.410 --> 00:45:27.820
my sincerest feelings for you.

00:45:27.820 --> 00:45:32.580
nandomo sakebu kara ne

00:45:27.820 --> 00:45:32.580
I'll shout them out however many times I need to.

00:45:32.580 --> 00:45:36.550
shinjite susumou

00:45:32.580 --> 00:45:36.550
'Cause they're true to my heart.

00:45:37.170 --> 00:45:41.670
kimi ga matteru

00:45:37.170 --> 00:45:41.670
'Cause they're waiting for you.

00:45:42.590 --> 00:45:46.720
ureshii sugiru yo

00:45:42.590 --> 00:45:46.720
'Cause I'm filled with joy.

00:45:47.970 --> 00:45:52.720
kimi wo matteru

00:45:47.970 --> 00:45:52.720
'Cause I'm waiting for you.
